Subject: [PATCH 11153/11362] [worktree] Read the redirect ledger against its
 own control (REQ-ARC-WMTE-7030/7031/7032)

Round two of the ARC live-agent evaluation. Measured first, on the ledger as
merged 2026-09-04 (14 receipts, 31 redirects) and the 14 eval artifacts in
results/arc_leaderboard_eval_runs/ (28 rows), all read-only.

What was wrong, and is now fixed:

1. The new-arm trigger was narrower than its concept (REQ-7030). It compared
   the fired arms against set(ARM_ORDER), which holds the env-gated,
   default-OFF tool rung (REQ-6760, 2026-08-29). A default run could never
   satisfy it. It reported 1 exhausted cell (11 windows) and hid 4 cells
   (53 of 64 unredirected windows). The receipt now names `arms_enabled`
   and the trigger reads that set; legacy rows fall back to the three
   default-on arms. Re-ingest: 5 cells, 64 windows.

2. The count said "propose an arm" 64 times without saying why the table
   ran dry (REQ-7031). Every exhausted window now records the state the
   supervisor saw: spent arms, attempt-cap and evidence-floor flags, goal
   bias, diversity. Bounded at 64 rows per receipt with a dropped counter.
   The ledger keeps the rows; each cell carries a per-flag summary; the
   heartbeat shows the count in flight.

3. Shadow receipts were counted and thrown away (REQ-7032). The shadow run
   r11l-3114878 leveled up at action 813 with nothing applied, and its
   would-have rows at 120/240/360 carry the same 765/645/525 that four
   applied runs booked as `helped`. Shadow receipts now ingest into a
   separate `controls` pool (never `entries`; REQ-6720 rule 1 holds). A
   credit a control reproduces reads `control_matched`; the report shows
   `helped_beyond_control`. On the live ledger: 12 of 19 credits are
   matched; 2/2/2/1 remain across the four arms. The frozen rules still
   key on pooled `helped` (as REQ-7013-D recorded).

Null results, stated as such: `co_credited_count` / `arm_credit` appear in
0 of 28 eval rows (the one post-merge run started before the merge), so
retire-or-promote by sole credit is not decidable on any existing evidence.
0 of 28 rows carry wall_s, run_envelope or solve_provenance: no run has
exercised the 2026-09-04/05 instrumentation yet.

Deliberately not done: no fifth arm (every cell is a legacy row with no
recorded exhaustion state; the candidates are ranked in the note for the
operator), no arm retired or promoted, no GPU run, no change to the
planning gate.

Proof: 21 tests (20 in test_arc_supervisor_exhaustion_20260905.py, 1 in
the heartbeat file, placed there because importing the eval script inside
a test trips the memory watchdog). 12 of 12 mutations RED with sha256
byte-identical restores, scored only after a green unmutated baseline and
re-confirmed green after the last restore. Step 6 of the error lifecycle:
the widened trigger IS the check; the exhaustion rows make the next
"propose an arm" decision rest on recorded state, not a hand-read receipt.

Mutation-gate markers retired deliberately (two, both gitignored under
ops/.test_suite_mutation_runs/). Each listed only paths the gate itself
marked [NOT this run]: spec.md edited by hand while the mutation harness
ran its pytest windows; the ledger re-ingested by the refine CLI, and
changelog.md and status.md edited by hand, while the whole-tree
--collect-only ran. No test wrote any of them. The ledger diff was checked
against HEAD: all 14 entries byte-equal, only the `controls` key added.

Whole-tree --collect-only: 61,601 tests, 7 collection errors, none in this
change: 4 x `No module named carnot._rust` (the PyO3 extension is not built
under a worktree PYTHONPATH pin) and 3 x the un-collectable
experiment_6814/6819/6828 test files already known.

